# =============================================================================
# Push EVERYTHING (code, data, debate logs, results, figures, tables, caches)
# EXCEPT the virtual environment and machine-generated junk.
# =============================================================================

# --- Virtual environments (the big thing we deliberately drop) ---
venv/
.venv/
env/

# --- Python bytecode / build junk ---
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.egg-info/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*.ipynb_checkpoints

# --- Secrets / local env ---
.env

# --- OS junk ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Oversized raw server logs -----------------------------------------------
# results/logs/ollama_gpu0.log is a ~239 MB Ollama server stdout dump; it
# exceeds GitHub's 100 MB per-file hard limit and is operational noise, not
# research data. Excluded so `git push` succeeds. (Use Git LFS if you must
# version it.) All other (small) run logs in results/logs/ ARE kept.
results/logs/ollama_*.log

# NOTE: data/raw, data/processed, data/debate_logs, results/{tables,figures,
# cache,logs} are intentionally NOT ignored — they are pushed in full.
